<title>UK: RESEARCH ALERT-Lehman cuts Commerzbank.</title>
<headline>RESEARCH ALERT-Lehman cuts Commerzbank.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-01-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Germany's Commerzbank AG was cut to &quot;underperform&quot; from &quot;neutral&quot; at Lehman Brothers, a research note from analyst Robert Law at the brokerage said on Friday.  </p>
<p>Law said Commerzbank had a similar business mix to its two larger domestic competitors but lacked their size and resources.</p>
<p>He said the stock included a &quot;substantial speculative premium&quot; and that recent strength should be used as an opportunity to reduce holdings.</p>
<p>The stock was down 18 pfennigs at 43.45 marks.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 5106</p>
